        "original_id": "aa543904-d0d8-5255-ba7a-1ce3f5c5da63",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Le piccole storie, \"Le Lit 29\", The Tragedy of Julius Caesar, Coriolanus, Antony and Cleopatra\n- People: Guy de Maupassant, William Shakespeare\n- Topics: Roman history, literary adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare is believed to have written The Tragedy of Julius Caesar in 1599.\n- Guy de Maupassant wrote the 1884 short story \"Le Lit 29\".\n- The Tragedy of Julius Caesar is a tragedy by William Shakespeare.\n- The Tragedy of Julius Caesar is one of several William Shakespeare plays based on true events from Roman history.\n- William Shakespeare's other plays based on true events from Roman history include Coriolanus and Antony and Cleopatra.\n- Some episodes of Le piccole storie are loosely based on Guy de Maupassant's \"Le Lit 29\" and on William Shakespeare's play The Tragedy of Julius Caesar.",
